      "revision": 1360611461,
      "text": "Momordica foetida is a perennial climbing vine native of tropical Africa, closely related to the bitter melon and balsam apple. Its species name (\"bad-smelling\") refers to its unpleasant smell. It was previously named M. morkorra and M. cordata (Cogn.)"
